jobs.description:
Klaas Puul BV has been one of Europe’s leading producers of fresh and frozen shrimp products for decades. From processing and packaging to delivery to our customers, Klaas Puul manages a large part of the production process in-house. Thanks to our advanced production system, craftsmanship, and strong focus on quality, we deliver high-quality shrimp products every day. Would you like to work for an organization recognized for its success? KP is one of the finalists of the North Holland Entrepreneur Awards 2026, a great recognition of our ambition, innovation, and entrepreneurial culture.

For our production department, we are looking for an enthusiastic and motivated;

Production Worker (full-time)

Are you looking for a varied role in a production environment? Do you enjoy taking responsibility and working together with colleagues? Then the position of Production Worker at Klaas Puul could be the right fit for you!

Please note: only candidates who are currently living in the Netherlands can apply.

In this role, you will be involved in a variety of activities across production, logistics, and cleaning. You will, for example, assist with packaging our shrimp and perform other tasks that contribute to an efficient production process. Hygiene and safety are key priorities, and you will ensure that your work is always carried out in accordance with the applicable guidelines.

You will work a fixed shift of your choice:

  - Morning/Afternoon Shift: 06:00 – 14:30

  - Afternoon/Evening Shift: 14:30 – 22:30

What do you bring?

  - MBO-level work and thinking skills;

  - 0–2 years of relevant work experience, preferably in a production or logistics environment;

  - You currently live in the Netherlands; applications from abroad will not be considered;

  - You are proactive, work hygienically and accurately, and are a true team player;

  - Good verbal and written communication skills in English; Dutch is a plus;

  - A valid forklift certificate is a plu

Are you passionate about quality, compliance and continuous improvement?Do you enjoy optimizing processes and ensuring that quality standards are maintained throughout an organization? Then this position as Quality Specialist could be the perfect next step in your career.

What will you do?

As a Quality Specialist, you will be responsible for managing, maintaining and continuously improving the Quality Management System (QMS). You will support site management, ensure compliance with customer and regulatory requirements, and help create a strong quality culture across the organization.

Your responsibilities include:

- Planning, implementing and maintaining the Quality Management System (QMS);
- Ensuring quality governance and compliance across logistics operations;
- Promoting a strong culture of quality and continuous improvement;
- Coordinating internal and external audits and following up on improvement actions;
- Monitoring customer, legal and third-party quality requirements;
- Identifying improvement opportunities and supporting process optimization;
- Advising and supporting management and operational teams on quality-related matters.

What do you bring?

- Proven experience in quality management within a logistics or operational environment;
- Knowledge of Quality Management Systems (QMS) and audit methodologies;
- Experience with compliance and continuous improvement;
- Strong analytical and communication skills;
- A proactive, structured and detail-oriented mindset;
- Good command of the English language.
